t.\n-  Molar relationship either Class I, < ½ unit Class II or Class III.\n-  Extraction of all four first premolar teeth as part of orthodontic treatment.\n-  Maximum anchorage required using mini-implant.\n-  No systemic disease.\n-  Good oral hygiene.\n-  No periodontal disease.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "AND": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "raw_text": "- Aged 18 years and above at the start of the treatment.",\n                          "Age": [\n                            "Aged"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Comparison": [\n                            "18 years and above"\n                          ],\n                          "Procedure": [\n                            "treatment"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Value": [\n                            "18"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Temporal-Unit": [\n                            "years"\n                          ],\n                          "Eq-Operator": [\n                            "and above"\n                          ]\n                        },\n                        "right": {\n                          "OR": {\n                            "left": {\n                              "raw_text": "- Molar relationship either Class I, < ½ unit Class II",\n                              "Observation": [\n                                "Molar relationship"\n                              ],\n                              "Eq-Comparison": [\n                                "Class I, < ½ unit Class II"\n                              ],\n                              "Observation-Name": [\n                                "Molar relationship"\n           